# Node / JS (workspace prototype frontend)
# `node_modules` carries no trailing slash on purpose. A `node_modules/`
# rule matches only a real directory, so a worktree sharing the main
# checkout's modules through a SYMLINK of that name was not ignored — and
# once such a link got committed (a private commit / that pull request, pointing at itself)
# every `npm run` in a checkout carrying it died with ELOOP, which is how
# husky's pre-commit came to fail for reasons unrelated to the staged
# change. Matching the bare name covers directory, symlink and
# not-yet-on-disk alike. Safe because no tracked path has a
# `node_modules` component, so nothing under that name needs un-ignoring
# (tests/test_repo_hygiene.py pins both of those halves).
node_modules
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts

# Secrets and local env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

